  "claude": [
    {
      "id": "claude-1",
      "date": 1781172800000,
      "content": "You wrote \"se prendre\" with the translation \"to get lost\" — that's not right. \"Se prendre\" means \"to take oneself\" and is used in expressions like s'en prendre à quelqu'un (to take it out on someone).\n\nThe word you want is \"se perdre\" — to get lost. And your usage sentence should be: Je me suis perdu dans le quartier.\n\nAlso \"prender\" is not a French word — the verb is \"perdre\". Easy to mix up when you're still building muscle memory for the vocabulary.",
      "tags": [
        "correction",
        "vocabulaire"
      ]
    }
  ]
}